selector_to_html = {"a[href=\"#errors\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Errors<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#errors\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Naming a quantity that does not exist, or one that is not available in that\nslot, raises <a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/design_inputs/DesignInputError.html#pyskyfire.regen.design_inputs.DesignInputError\" title=\"pyskyfire.regen.design_inputs.DesignInputError\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">DesignInputError</span></code></a> when\nthe owning object is constructed. The message names the offending parameter,\nsays why it was refused, and lists what is legal there:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/thrust_chamber/CoolingCircuit.html#pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.CoolingCircuit\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.CoolingCircuit\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">CoolingCircuit</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">contour</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">cross_section</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">span</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/stdtypes.html#list\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">list</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">[</span></span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">]</span></span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">placement</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">channel_height</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">walls</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">coolant_transport</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">roughness</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">hot_gas_surface_area_multiplier</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">outer_walls</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">enable_fin</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rib_material</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Simulation-only representation of a cooling circuit.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">walls</span></code> are ordered from hot gas to coolant. Any <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">role=\"liner\"</span></code>\nlayers precede the main layers; at least one main layer is required.\nWall-like objects without a role are treated as main layers.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">enable_fin=True</span></code> enables this circuit\u2019s rib/fin heat-transfer model.\n<code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">rib_material</span></code> optionally supplies its material (with <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">get_k(T)</span></code>).\nWhen omitted, the coolant-facing main-wall material is used. Disabling\nfins removes their thermal enhancement, not their channel geometry.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#why-the-tiers-exist\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Why the tiers exist<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#why-the-tiers-exist\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>The available quantities differ from one argument to the next because the\ngeometry is built in a fixed order, and each step consumes what the previous\nones produced:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/channel_placement/SurfacePlacement.html#pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.SurfacePlacement\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.SurfacePlacement\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">SurfacePlacement</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n_channel_positions</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">helix_angle</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">channel_angular_width</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ChannelPlacement</span></code></p><p>Placement model for surface-mounted cooling channels.</p><p>Channels are positioned just outside the main wall stack,\noffset by total thickness and corrected for local contour angle.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#where-design-inputs-are-accepted\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Where design inputs are accepted<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#where-design-inputs-are-accepted\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Every one of these also accepts a plain <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></code>, which is the same as a\nfunction that takes no parameters and returns that number.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">sidewall_half_thickness</span></code> means one complete sidewall of an isolated tube, or\nhalf of the shared rib between neighbouring chamber channels. Two 0.5 mm\nsidewalls form a 1 mm shared rib. Exposure fractions range from 0 to 1;\nexposure angles use radians. Local exchanger profiles expose their path\ncoordinate as <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">x</span></code>; chamber-only quantities require a chamber context.</p>", "a[href=\"#glossary\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Glossary<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#glossary\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>Every quantity a design input may name, exhaustively.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/thrust_chamber/ThrustChamber.html#pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.ThrustChamber\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.ThrustChamber\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">ThrustChamber</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">contour</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">cooling_circuits</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">combustion_transport</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">optimal_values</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">K_factor</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.3</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n_nodes</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">50</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">h_gas_corr</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">h_cold_corr</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#float\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">float</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">1.0</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">compute_gas</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">True</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">film_cooling</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/thrust_chamber/FilmCooling.html#pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.FilmCooling\" title=\"pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.FilmCooling\"><span class=\"pre\">FilmCooling</span></a><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">|</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/constants.html#None\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">keep_outs</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Simulation-only thrust-chamber assembly.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/contour/Contour.html#pyskyfire.regen.contour.Contour\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.contour.Contour\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.contour.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Contour</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">xs</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">rs</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">chamber_angle</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">nozzle_angle</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Inner hot-gas contour of a bell-type rocket engine.</p><p>Represents the geometric wall line from the start of the chamber to\nthe nozzle exit, providing local areas, slopes, and radii.</p><p class=\"rubric\">Notes</p><p>This class is used by higher-level objects such as\n<code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">CoolingCircuit</span></code> and\n<code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ThrustChamber</span></code>.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#tier-c-the-resolved-section\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Tier C \u2014 the resolved section<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#tier-c-the-resolved-section\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p>For rounded sections, <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">height_input=\"base\"</span></code> restores the older base-height\nparameter. Design-input functions requesting <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">h</span></code> receive that supplied value;\nthe algebraic <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">r_channel_top</span></code> and <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">pitch_mid</span></code> quantities above use it too.\nThe height report defaults to the converted full internal height. See\n<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"channel-construction.html\"><span class=\"doc\">Physical cooling-channel construction</span></a> for conversion and plotting examples. Keeping <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">h</span></code>\nin its input convention also lets helix laws use it before the angular pitch\nneeded for full-height conversion has been resolved.</p><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">r_channel_base</span></code> is resolved geometry, not <code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">r</span> <span class=\"pre\">+</span> <span class=\"pre\">t_wall</span></code>: the section stands off\nthe contour along its normal, so a sloping wall projects the stack outward, and\na rounded section\u2019s base point is the lobe centre its gas-area constraint\nsolves for. Before the section has been placed \u2014 while a height or helix law is\nbeing evaluated \u2014 it falls back to the contour radius.</p>", "a[href=\"../howto/area-preserving-helix.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Hold the coolant area constant with a helix<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#hold-the-coolant-area-constant-with-a-helix\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>A squared channel of fixed height, rib width and count gets wider wherever the\nwall it wraps gets wider. On an engine with area ratio 8, an axial channel\nbuilt this way has more than three times the throat area at the nozzle exit. To\nkeep the area constant, wind the channel into a helix that steepens as the\nradius grows. The extra circumference then goes into the winding instead of the\nchannel width.</p><p>This guide finds that helix by root-finding the helix angle against the area\nPyskyfire computes. The result below has 40 channels, each holding the same\ncoolant area to within one part in a million from the injector to the nozzle\nexit. Drag to rotate, scroll to zoom and right-drag to pan.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/channel_placement/InternalPlacement.html#pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.InternalPlacement\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.InternalPlacement\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.channel_placement.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">InternalPlacement</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n_channel_positions</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n_channels_per_leaf</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#int\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">int</span></a></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">channel_angular_width</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">occludes</span></span><span class=\"p\"><span class=\"pre\">:</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\"><a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/functions.html#bool\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><span class=\"pre\">bool</span></a></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">False</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">helix_angle</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">0.0</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ChannelPlacement</span></code></p><p>Placement model for in-wall or in-chamber heat-exchanger channels.</p><p>Allows multiple stacked channels per angular leaf and optional\nuser-defined angular-width laws.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/design_inputs/DesignInputError.html#pyskyfire.regen.design_inputs.DesignInputError\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.design_inputs.DesignInputError\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">exception</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.design_inputs.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">DesignInputError</span></span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <a class=\"reference external\" href=\"https://docs.python.org/3/builtins/exceptions.html#ValueError\" title=\"(in Python v3.15)\"><code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ValueError</span></code></a></p><p>Raised when a design-input function cannot be dispatched or evaluated.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"#tier-a-contour\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Tier A \u2014 contour<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#tier-a-contour\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3>", "a[href=\"#examples\"]": "<h2 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Examples<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#examples\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h2><p>A wall that thins from 1.2 mm in the chamber to 0.8 mm at the exit, using the\nnormalised axial coordinate rather than absolute metres:</p>", "a[href=\"#tier-b-layout-and-walls\"]": "<h3 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Tier B \u2014 layout and walls<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#tier-b-layout-and-walls\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h3><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">n_channels_all_circuits</span></code> is the one quantity a circuit cannot work out alone,\nbecause it counts channels belonging to other circuits. It is available only\nonce the circuit has been given to a\n<a class=\"reference internal\" href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/thrust_chamber/ThrustChamber.html#pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.ThrustChamber\" title=\"pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.ThrustChamber\"><code class=\"xref py py-class docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ThrustChamber</span></code></a>.</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/thrust_chamber/Wall.html#pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.Wall\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.Wall\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.thrust_chamber.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">Wall</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">material</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">thickness</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">name</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">role</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'main'</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Single structural wall or coating layer in a thrust chamber.</p><p>Encapsulates material and thickness information for heat-conduction\ncalculations.</p></dd>", "a[href=\"channel-construction.html\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Physical cooling-channel construction<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#physical-cooling-channel-construction\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p><code class=\"docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">build_channel_construction(circuit,</span> <span class=\"pre\">reference_path)</span></code> resolves a circuit\u2019s\nnominal winding into the section it physically occupies. The same resolved\ngeometry feeds the simulation, CAD, and the native 3D viewer, so a channel is\nsized once and drawn, meshed and solved from that one answer.</p>", "a[href=\"#design-input-functions\"]": "<h1 class=\"tippy-header\" style=\"margin-top: 0;\">Design-Input Functions<a class=\"headerlink\" href=\"#design-input-functions\" title=\"Link to this heading\">\u00b6</a></h1><p>Most of the geometry you hand to Pyskyfire can be either a number or a\nfunction. A wall can be 1 mm thick everywhere, or it can thin out towards the\nnozzle exit. A rib can be 1 mm wide everywhere, or it can always take up a\nfifth of the local channel pitch.</p><p>A function used this way is called a <strong>design input</strong>. It declares the\nquantities it needs <em>by parameter name</em>, and Pyskyfire supplies exactly those:</p>", "a[href=\"../autoapi/pyskyfire/regen/cross_section/CrossSectionSquared.html#pyskyfire.regen.cross_section.CrossSectionSquared\"]": "<dt class=\"sig sig-object py\" id=\"pyskyfire.regen.cross_section.CrossSectionSquared\">\n<span class=\"property\"><span class=\"k\"><span class=\"pre\">class</span></span><span class=\"w\"> </span></span><span class=\"sig-prename descclassname\"><span class=\"pre\">pyskyfire.regen.cross_section.</span></span><span class=\"sig-name descname\"><span class=\"pre\">CrossSectionSquared</span></span><span class=\"sig-paren\">(</span><em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">sidewall_half_thickness</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">n_points</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">8</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"keyword-only-separator o\"><abbr title=\"Keyword-only parameters separator (PEP 3102)\"><span class=\"pre\">*</span></abbr></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">roof_thickness</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">floor</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'arc'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">roof</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">'arc'</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">exposure</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">None</span></span></em>, <em class=\"sig-param\"><span class=\"n\"><span class=\"pre\">enable_fin</span></span><span class=\"o\"><span class=\"pre\">=</span></span><span class=\"default_value\"><span class=\"pre\">False</span></span></em><span class=\"sig-paren\">)</span></dt><dd><p>Bases: <code class=\"xref py py-obj docutils literal notranslate\"><span class=\"pre\">ChannelSection</span></code></p><p>Squared passages with independently straight or curved floor and roof.</p><p>sidewall_half_thickness [m] is ONE tube sidewall\u2019s normal thickness,\nequivalent to HALF the shared rib between adjacent chamber channels. A\nconstant or design-input callable is accepted. A former 1 mm full rib is\ntherefore specified as 0.5 mm here.</p><p>Floor thickness comes from SectionProfiles.t_wall. roof_thickness defaults\nto that thickness and may instead be a constant or callable. floor and roof\nindependently accept \u201carc\u201d or \u201cline\u201d. Direct width profiles use the\ndistance between internal sidewall endpoints. With sector profiles, the\nexisting constant-material-width rib construction determines those\nendpoints; choosing a line joins the same endpoints with a chord.</p></dd>"}
skip_classes = ["headerlink", "sd-stretched-link"]

window.onload = function () {
    for (const [select, tip_html] of Object.entries(selector_to_html)) {
        const links = document.querySelectorAll(` ${select}`);
        for (const link of links) {
            if (skip_classes.some(c => link.classList.contains(c))) {
                continue;
            }

            tippy(link, {
                content: tip_html,
                allowHTML: true,
                arrow: true,
                placement: 'auto-start', maxWidth: 600, interactive: false,
                onShow(instance) {MathJax.typesetPromise([instance.popper]).then(() => {});},
            });
        };
    };
    console.log("tippy tips loaded!");
};
